#{[17592186480107 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186480101 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186480107 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186480107 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $g(x)=4{e}^{x}-2{x}^{2}+6x+8$, find the slope of the tangent at $x=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186480107 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fc8205dd-9383-5240-aa7c-245bff3c1e94" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186480107 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the addition and the power rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{e}^{x}-2{x}^{2}+6x+8) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{e}^{x})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(8) \\\\  & =4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+6\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(8) \\\\  & =4{e}^{x}-2(2x)+6(1)+0 \\\\  & =4{e}^{x}-4x+6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=0$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=0} & ={(4{e}^{x}-4x+6)\\,|}_{x=0} \\\\  & =4{e}^{0}-4\\cdot 0+6 \\\\  & =4\\cdot 1+0+6 \\\\  & =4+6 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186480109 #edb/ref 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186096611.py" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186480109 #edb/ref 1169 #uuid "337ca211-135e-5973-81fe-043f1cf73b4b" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186542624 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186543608 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542624 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186543656 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542624 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186543657 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542624 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186543663 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542624 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186543676 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542624 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542624 #edb/ref 1045 "Differentiating Exponential Functions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542624 #