325821-aed1-5216-b5a3-ffaf528190d5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543477 #edb/ref 1074 "Applying the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)-3\\cdot {2}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5))-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3\\cdot {2}^{x}) \\\\  & =0-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({2}^{x}) \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)\\cdot {2}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & ={(-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)\\cdot {2}^{x})|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)\\cdot {2}^{1} \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543497 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186543424 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543497 #edb/ref 1069 "q-340277" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543497 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543497 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $f(x)=3\\cdot {4}^{x}-2{e}^{x}$, the slope of the tangent at $x=1$ is{{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543497 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "47d673bd-5b90-569f-9bcd-5db84649c548" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543497 #edb/ref 1074 "Applying the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3\\cdot {4}^{x}-2{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3\\cdot {4}^{x})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({4}^{x})-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x}) \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)\\cdot {4}^{x}-2{e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & ={(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)\\cdot {4}^{x}-2{e}^{x})|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)\\cdot {4}^{1}-2{e}^{1} \\\\  & =12\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)-2e.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543507 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186543349 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543507 #edb/ref 1069 "q-340285" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543507 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543507 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $f(x)=5\\cdot {7}^{x}$, the slope of the tangent at $x=0$ is{{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543507 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5e010595-5a96-5d35-8548-77ec2815a5a0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543507 #edb/ref 1074 "Applying the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5\\cdot {7}^{x}) \\\\  & =5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({7}^{x}) \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)\\cdot {7}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=0$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=0} & ={(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)\\cdot {7}^{x})|}_{x=0} \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)\\cdot {7}^{0} \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543608 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186543656 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543608 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1be5bca1-959e-5dc6-afbd-3797a27d03d0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543608 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186543477 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543656 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "af2c57ec-5158-512f-86f1-2fb4d3101440" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543656 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186543507 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543657 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186543676 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543657 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b6c1d9da-40dd-56ff-9485-773b66c48f3c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543657 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186096989 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543663 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186543608 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543663 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c9a5a8b7-be4a-5735-b51b-59b6b55d6cc5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543663 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186543497 #edb/ref 175921860454